From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:23:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 3106 (speed): a saved row touches its thread in the same
 round trip

Every saved row used to send a second statement to mark its thread as
touched. The [post-run] lines put each round trip at ~145 ms, and an answer
with one tool turn saves four rows, so that second statement cost ~0.6 s of
every answer. The INSERT and the UPDATE now go as one statement (a
data-modifying CTE always runs), so the thread is touched exactly as before.
Checked against Postgres 16 with untyped parameters, as node-pg sends them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
